s the problem.\n- Ship a virtual DOM library. Rejected: it re-renders whole trees, and\n  it does not know about microtags hosts or the server's markup.\n- Re-render regions by assigning `innerHTML`. Rejected: it recreates\n  hosts, losing their state and identity.\n\n## Decision\n\nThe core entry exports `Signal` and `Serialized<T>` as types.\n`Serialized<T>` is a shallow unwrap: each property that is a signal\nbecomes its value type, and other properties pass through. No runtime\nserialization helper ships in the library.\n\nEvery host gets a property accessor for each declared prop. Assigning a\nplain value writes the prop; assigning a signal makes the prop read\nthrough to it. A property set before upgrade is picked up at upgrade.\nThis is the only runtime change to the core entry.\n\n`microtags/htm` gains a second module, selected by the `browser` export\ncondition. The import specifier is the same on both sides, with no\nruntime environment check. `html` returns opaque **markup** on both\nsides instead of a string. Server markup converts to its HTML with\n`String()`. Markup, render output, and `raw` stay trusted, so nesting\nnever double-escapes.\n\nOn the server, a signal or function in a hole is evaluated once. In\nchild position its output is wrapped in `<!--[-->` and `<!--]-->`\nmarkers, and so are children passed to a component. A function-valued\n`on<event>` prop is omitted. A page with no reactive holes and no\ncomponent children renders the same bytes as before.\n\nIn the browser, holes bind by position:\n\n- A signal as a component prop is assigned to the host's prop accessor.\n- A signal or function as an attribute on a plain element is bound to\n  that attribute; `false`, `null`, or `undefined` removes it.\n- A signal or function in child position is a **reactive region**.\n- `on<event>` with a function becomes a listener.\n- Anything else is static.\n\n`mount(container, markup)` **adopts** existing children: it walks the\nmarkup against the DOM in document order, binds, and creates no nodes.\nAn empty container gets new nodes. It returns a dispose function that\nstops effects and removes listeners, leaving the DOM in place. Mounting\ntwice on one container throws.\n\nHosts are opaque. Adoption and reconciliation never descend into a\nhost's own markup, only into its marked children range, if any.\n\nWhen a region re-evaluates, its old nodes are morphed toward the new\nmarkup. Keyed children are matched by `key` and moved; unkeyed children\nare matched by position and tag name and patched. A matching host is\nkept and its props rebound, never recreated.\n\nStripping is unchanged. Creating a component whose render link was\nstripped throws an error naming the tag and pointing at `client: true`\nand the build-time keep list. An adoption mismatch on tag name warns in\ndevelopment and leaves that server subtree untouched.\n\n## Trade-offs\n\nApp code gets one state object and no manual DOM work, at the cost of a\nlarger templater subpath. Consumers who do not import `microtags/htm`\npay nothing; the core entry grows only by the prop accessors.\n\nValue updates go straight through signals with no diffing. Only\nstructural changes (conditionals, lists) pay for a morph, and only over\nthe affected region.\n\nChanging the return type of `html` from string to markup is a breaking\nchange. It is acceptable at 0.0.x, and callers convert explicitly.\n\nComment markers add a few bytes to server output where reactivity is\nused, and nothing where it is not.\n\nTreating hosts as opaque keeps reconciliation simple and leaves a\ncomponent's internals to its own setup, but a region cannot patch inside\na host's markup.\n\n## Consequences\n\nADR-004 is relaxed for the templater subpath only. Its size-limit entry\nis raised to the measured result, and the browser build gets its own\nentry so growth stays visible. The core entry stays budgeted as before.\n\nADR-005 still holds: render links are stripped by default. A component\ncreated in the browser, for example as a list item, must be kept with\n`client: true` or the keep list.\n\nAfter a signal is assigned to a prop accessor, the host's attribute no\nlonger tracks the current value. Tests and docs must read the property,\nnot the attribute.\n\nThe package gains a fourth browser build script and a `browser`\ncondition on the `./htm` export. Bundler aliases that point\n`microtags/htm` at source must make the same split.\n\nThis ADR supersedes no earlier decision. ADR-008 records how the\nhydration example uses it.\nimport type { StandardSchemaV1 } from '@standard-schema/spec'\nimport type { Markup } from './htm.js'\nimport type {\n    PropDef,\n    PropType,\n    PropertyOnlyProp,\n    SetupContext,\n    Coercer,\n    RefDef,\n    SingleRefDef,\n    MultipleRefDef,\n    RefsMap,\n    ContextToken,\n    ContextsMap,\n} from './types.js'\nimport {\n    coerceNumber,\n    coerceString,\n    coerceBoolean,\n    coerceJson,\n} from './util.js'\nimport { factory } from './factory.js'\nexport type PropKind = 'prop-only' | 'schema' | 'coercer'\n\nexport interface PropMeta {\n    kind:PropKind\n    coercer:Coercer<unknown>\n    serialize:(value:unknown) => string | null\n}\n\nconst _esc:Record<string, string> = {\n    '&': '&amp;',\n    '\"': '&quot;',\n    \"'\": '&#39;',\n    '<': '&lt;',\n    '>': '&gt;',\n}\nfunction _escAttr (s:string):string {\n    return s.replace(/[&\"'<>]/g, c => _esc[c])\n}\n\nfunction _sNull ():null { return null }\nfunction _sStr (v:unknown):string | null {\n    return v == null ? null : String(v)\n}\nfunction _sBool (v:unknown):string | null {\n    return v === true ? '' : null\n}\nfunction _sJson (v:unknown):string | null {\n    return v == null ? null : JSON.stringify(v)\n}\n\nfunction _serializerFor (\n    c:Coercer<unknown>, k:PropKind\n):(v:unknown) => string | null {\n    if (k === 'prop-only') return _sNull\n    if (k === 'schema') return _sStr\n    if (c === coerceBoolean) return _sBool\n    if (c === coerceJson) return _sJson\n    return _sStr\n}\n\nfunction _renderHost (\n    tag:string, metas:Record<string, PropMeta>,\n    props:Record<string, unknown>,\n    extra:Record<string, string> | undefined,\n    inner:string\n):string {\n    let a = ''\n    for (const [k, m] of Object.entries(metas)) {\n        if (!(k in props)) continue\n        const s = m.serialize(props[k])\n        if (s === null) continue\n        a += s === '' ? ` ${k}` : ` ${k}=\"${_escAttr(s)}\"`\n    }\n    if (extra) {\n        for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(extra)) {\n            a += v === '' ? ` ${k}` : ` ${k}=\"${_escAttr(v)}\"`\n        }\n    }\n    return `<${tag}${a}>${inner}</${tag}>`\n}\n\n/** The DSL object passed to the withProps callback. */\nexport type PropDSL = {\n    number():Coercer<number>\n    string():Coercer<string>\n    boolean():Coercer<boolean>\n    json<T>():Coercer<T | undefined>\n    schema<T>(validator:StandardSchemaV1<unknown, T>):StandardSchemaV1<unknown, T>\n    prop<T>(initial:T):PropertyOnlyProp<T>\n}\n\nexport const propDSL:PropDSL = {\n    number: () => coerceNumber,\n    string: () => coerceString,\n    boolean: () => coerceBoolean,\n    json: <T>() => coerceJson as Coercer<T | undefined>,\n    schema: <T>(v:StandardSchemaV1<unknown, T>) => v,\n    prop: <T>(initial:T):PropertyOnlyProp<T> => (\n        { _microtag: 'prop', initial }\n    ),\n}\n\n/**\n * DSL object passed to the withRefs callback.\n * Call `r.one()` for a single element or `r.all()` for multiple. Pass a\n * CSS selector to query by it, or omit it to match `[data-ref=\"<key>\"]`.\n *\n * Element typing:\n * - `r.one()` defaults to `HTMLElement`.\n * - `r.one<T>()` sets the type and keeps the `[data-ref]` selector.\n * - `r.one('button')` infers the type from the tag AND queries by that\n *   tag, exactly like `document.querySelector('button')`.\n */\nexport type RefsDSL = {\n    one<K extends keyof HTMLElementTagNameMap>(\n        selector:K\n    ):SingleRefDef<HTMLElementTagNameMap[K]>\n    one<T extends HTMLElement = HTMLElement>(selector?:string):SingleRefDef<T>\n\n    all<K extends keyof HTMLElementTagNameMap>(\n        selector:K\n    ):MultipleRefDef<HTMLElementTagNameMap[K]>\n    all<T extends HTMLElement = HTMLElement>(selector?:string):MultipleRefDef<T>\n}\n\nexport const refsDSL:RefsDSL = {\n    one: ((selector?:string):SingleRefDef => (\n        { _microtag: 'ref:one', selector }\n    )) as RefsDSL['one'],\n    all: ((selector?:string):MultipleRefDef => (\n        { _microtag: 'ref:all', selector }\n    )) as RefsDSL['all'],\n}\n\n/**\n * DSL object passed to the withContexts callback.\n * Currently a no-op placeholder; the user references imported\n * context tokens directly in the returned record.\nsrc/factory.ts:26: * real HTMLElement; in Node (e.g. reading `.TAG` for SSR) it falls back\nsrc/builders.ts:63:function _renderHost (\nsrc/builders.ts:155:/** Plain values for props (not signals) in the render context. */\nsrc/builders.ts:166:    TAG:string\nsrc/builders.ts:198: * the tag name it was registered under (`TAG`) and the names of its\nsrc/builders.ts:208:    readonly TAG:string\nsrc/builders.ts:215:    readonly render:StaticRenderFn<Props>\nsrc/builders.ts:234:    private readonly _renderFn?:RenderFn<Props, RefDefs>\nsrc/builders.ts:252:        this._renderFn = renderFn as\nsrc/builders.ts:261:    get TAG ():string {\nsrc/builders.ts:325:            this._renderFn,\nsrc/builders.ts:341:            this._renderFn,\nsrc/builders.ts:345:    render (\nsrc/builders.ts:375:        Object.defineProperty(El, 'TAG', {\nsrc/builders.ts:394:        if (this._renderFn) {\nsrc/builders.ts:395:            const renderFn = this._renderFn\nsrc/builders.ts:411:                    TAG: tagName,\nsrc/builders.ts:415:                return _renderHost(\nsrc/builders.ts:426:            Object.defineProperty(El, 'render', {\nimport { test } from '@substrate-system/tapzero'\nimport type { StandardSchemaV1 } from '@standard-schema/spec'\nimport { signal, effect } from 'alien-signals'\nimport { peek, untracked, define } from '../src/index.js'\nimport { factory } from '../src/factory.js'\nimport { coerceNumber } from '../src/util.js'\nimport { ComponentBuilder } from '../src/builders.js'\nimport { createContext, provide } from '../src/context.js'\nimport type { ContextToken } from '../src/types.js'\nimport { render, renderList } from '../src/render.js'\nimport { html, raw } from '../src/htm.js'\nimport { reveal } from '../example-hydration/client/util.js'\n\ntest('placeholder test', t => {\n    t.ok(true, 'test harness is wired')\n})\n\ntest('peek reads a signal without subscribing', t => {\n    const count = signal(0)\n    let runs = 0\n\n    effect(() => {\n        runs++\n        // peek inside an effect should NOT create a subscription\n        peek(count)\n    })\n\n    t.equal(runs, 1, 'effect runs once on creation')\n\n    count(1)\n    t.equal(runs, 1, 'effect does NOT re-run when peeked signal changes')\n})\n\ntest('untracked reads do not create subscriptions', t => {\n    const a = signal(10)\n    let runs = 0\n\n    effect(() => {\n        runs++\n        untracked(() => a())\n    })\n\n    t.equal(runs, 1, 'effect runs once on creation')\n    a(20)\n    t.equal(runs, 1, 'effect does NOT re-run after untracked read')\n})\n\ntest('peek returns current signal value', t => {\n    const s = signal('hello')\n    t.equal(peek(s), 'hello', 'peek returns current value')\n    s('world')\n    t.equal(peek(s), 'world', 'peek returns updated value')\n})\n\ntest('untracked restores subscription context', t => {\n    const a = signal(0)\n    const b = signal(0)\n    let runs = 0\n\n    effect(() => {\n1:import { test } from '@substrate-system/tapzero'\n2:import type { StandardSchemaV1 } from '@standard-schema/spec'\n3:import { signal, effect } from 'alien-signals'\n4:import { peek, untracked, define } from '../src/index.js'\n5:import { factory } from '../src/factory.js'\n6:import { coerceNumber } from '../src/util.js'\n7:import { ComponentBuilder } from '../src/builders.js'\n8:import { createContext, provide } from '../src/context.js'\n9:import type { ContextToken } from '../src/types.js'\n10:import { render, renderList } from '../src/render.js'\n11:import { html, raw } from '../src/htm.js'\n12:import { reveal } from '../example-hydration/client/util.js'\n14:test('placeholder test', t => {\n18:test('peek reads a signal without subscribing', t => {\n34:test('untracked reads do not create subscriptions', t => {\n48:test('peek returns current signal value', t => {\n55:test('untracked restores subscription context', t => {\n75:test('define: registers a working custom element', t => {\n87:test('reactive props: reading, writing, and reacting', t => {\n119:test('factory: creates HTMLElement subclass with no shadow DOM', t => {\n133:test('factory: connectedCallback hydrates props from attributes', t => {\n150:test('factory: attributeChangedCallback updates prop signal', t => {\n171:test('factory: disconnectedCallback runs all registered cleanups', t => {\n189:test('factory: effects are disposed on disconnect', t => {\n213:test('factory: reconnecting re-runs setup with fresh scope', t => {\n236:test('factory: reconnect preserves programmatically-set prop values', t => {\n261:test('factory: cleanup errors: remaining cleanups run, first error re-throws', t => {\n294:test('withProps: p.number() hydrates number from attribute', t => {\n307:test('withProps: p.string() hydrates string from attribute', t => {\n320:test('withProps: p.boolean() coerces attribute presence', t => {\n344:test('withProps: p.json() parses attribute as JSON', t => {\n357:test('withProps: p.schema() accepts a Standard Schema validator', t => {\n383:test('withProps: p.prop() creates a property-only (non-observed) prop', t => {\n410:test('withProps: observed attributes react to attributeChangedCallback', t => {\n431:test('withRefs: r.one resolves single [data-ref] element', t => {\n446:test('withRefs: r.all resolves multiple [data-ref] elements', t => {\n466:test('withRefs: r.all returns empty array when no matches', t => {\n479:test('withRefs: r.one throws when ref element not found', t => {\n494:test('withRefs: r.one(selector) resolves by CSS selector', t => {\n508:test('withRefs: r.one(tag) resolves an element by tag name', t => {\n522:test('withRefs: r.all(selector) resolves multiple by CSS selector', t => {\n540:test('withContexts: context keys appear in ctx.contexts', t => {\n559:test('ctx.on: listener is called and auto-removed on disconnect', t => {\n578:test('ctx.emit: string form dispatches a bubbling CustomEvent with detail', t => {\n606:test('ctx.emit: Event form dispatches as-is; returns false when canceled', t => {\n636:test('ctx.bind: updates DOM property reactively, stops after disconnect', t => {\n658:test('ctx.bind: two-way text input writes user input to signal', t => {\n681:test('ctx.bind: checkbox auto-detects checked/change', t => {\n705:test('ctx.bind: getter one-way derives a property from a signal', t => {\n724:test('ctx.bind: number input auto-detects valueAsNumber/input', t => {\n748:test('ctx.peek: no subscription inside ctx.effect', t => {\n770:test('ctx.consume: returns undefined for unresolved context token', t => {\n789:test('define: setup() registers the custom element', t => {\n794:test('define: setup() returns the element class', t => {\n800:test('define: builder exposes TAG', t => {\n805:test('define: TAG is available after withProps/withRefs', t => {\n813:test('define: setup() element class exposes static TAG', t => {\n819:test('define: full chain registers and works', t => {\n831:test('withProps + withRefs + withContexts chain type-checks', t => {\n860:test('createContext: returns a token with a symbol id', t => {\n865:test('createContext: each token has a unique id', t => {\n871:test('provide + withContexts: value available in ctx.contexts', t => {\n889:test('deferred setup: setup waits until context resolves', t => {\n910:test('context reactivity: effect re-runs when context value changes', t => {\n940:test('ctx.consume: reads optional context value from ancestor', t => {\n971:test('render: stamps template into container', t => {\n983:test('render: calling render again with same template reuses element', t => {\n1003:test('render: works with no options', t => {\n1010:test('renderList: renders items from data array', t => {\n1027:test('renderList: removes items no longer in data', t => {\n1046:test('renderList: reuses existing elements by key', t => {\n1069:test('attribute hydration: props initialized from attributes on connect', t => {\n1099:test('attributeChangedCallback: updates prop signal on attribute change', t => {\n1130:test('refs: r.one resolves single and r.all resolves multiple via define()', t => {\n1164:test('context: ctx.consume reads provided value from ancestor element', t => {\n1181:test('context: deferred setup waits for ALL required contexts', t => {\n1206:test('context: consumer effect re-runs when context value changes', t => {\n1242:test('untracked: reading inside ctx.effect does not create subscription', t => {\n1266:test('cleanup: ctx.on listener removed on disconnect', t => {\n1283:test('cleanup: ctx.effect disposed on disconnect', t => {","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
