{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfi6vimom8nzWhWGUh3LK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016u7M3UYBwB6m8tQr6HhsVk","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/nick/code/microtags.unidirectional-hydration-05-browser-templater-and-mount; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='AGENTS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nanchor=\"### Build entry (`src/build.ts`)\"\nnote='''### Browser templater (`src/htm.browser.ts`)\n\nSelected for `microtags/htm` by the `browser` export condition (listed\nfirst in `exports[\"./htm\"]`). It is built by the same three browser\nscripts as `src/htm.ts` and has its own `.size-limit.js` entry. Its\n`html` returns a `Markup` holding a node description (or `raw` HTML);\n`String(m)` still serializes to static HTML, so kept components'\nrender functions work in the browser. `mount` creates nodes inside an\n`effectScope`; creating a host calls its static `render` and parses the\nresult with `document.importNode`, which upgrades it synchronously.\n`RenderFn` accepts both `Markup` types. The example's Vite config\nsplits the import with a `resolveId` plugin keyed on `ssr`, and aliases\n`microtags` with an exact-match regex so it does not swallow\n`microtags/htm`. Browser tests import `../src/htm.browser.js` directly;\nthe resolution test lives in `test/plugins.ts` and needs `dist/`.\n\n'''\ns=s.replace(anchor, note+anchor,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnpm test 2>&1 | grep -E \"^not ok|# (pass|fail)|error TS\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":408,"cache_read_input_tokens":85857,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":408},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35e688ca-044a-4d38-b311-1